y for  a minute  and actually talk back to you guys now  so i guess  one of the main things that you have to  consider and be concerned about  when interviewing or being interviewed  is actually  bringing value to the team or bringing  value to the firm  standing on your own two feet with a  good portfolio is a good start  but being able to actually bring some  sort of value  to this firm and this team is incredibly  incredibly important that i can't stress  enough  i think from somebody hiring and being  on the other end of the table for the  first time ever  it was very difficult on my end to be  able to understand where these people  came from  but being able to isolate them from  their portfolios and  their enthusiasm in an interview  actually made it  a lot easier to be able to select  somebody to join the team  by having a good portfolio with  potentially just abstract ideas versus  solid construction knowledge and having  great enthusiasm to learn  to be wanting to be part of the team and  knowing a little bit about the firm and  the interview you're walking into  is incredibly valuable one of my  personal favorite interview questions is  what kind of hobbies do you have  and that's simply for me to fish out  what kind of other skill sets  you might be bringing to the table so  personally for me i ran all sorts of  different businesses  and loved photography videography social  media  all of that before i got into the  profession of architecture  so from my end i actually brought in  some sort of  marketing background into what was  previously  a non-marketing industry so if this  professional that you're interviewing  has some sort of  i guess background hobby where they like  to spend their time making youtube  videos  either taking photos taking videos doing  something creative  that might be able to be backtracked  into the firm  is an exceptional asset to have and a  great answer to be looking for  most of the time you'll get the simple  answer like i enjoy running or i enjoy  sport which are good answers it means  they get out they interact with the  community  however if you're looking for somebody  to actually bring value to the firm  you want to be looking for people that  have more than  your standard sport answers in these  interviews  one more thing to be mindful of is grads  are actually pretty thankful to get a  job straight out of uni or college  depending on where you're watching this  video  they have a tendency to be thankful for  that position  for a very long time it means they're  probably going to stick around in that  firm  for anywhere between three to five years  as a basic graduate  whilst there's other grads that are  extremely valuable to the firm  and are shown that they're valuable to  the firm in some way shape or form  being a financial remuneration or just  constant positive reinforcement  they might actually stick around for a  lifetime so that grad  may be the best hire you've had in a  very long time  yes i know you're not investing in a  very  knowledgeable educated technical  construction detailer but that's  probably not what you're looking for at  the start either  so if you're out there hiring a grad  these are some fundamental things that  you need to keep in the back of your  mind  because grads aren't just you're simple  easy to get  going and chuck them to do the basic  jobs nobody wants  even though most of them aware that  they're going to do that you don't  really  need to do that because these guys have  more skills  and are trained to be able to do things  that you probably haven't even thought  about  anyway that's all for me today guys  thanks so much for watching i hope you  enjoyed the video  if you did make sure you smash that like  button down below help this video with  the algorithm  and if you want to see more of my  content smash that subscribe button  and as always i will see you next monday

